>>And some notes:
I got extremely lucky in this game. The first part was mostly
uneventful, but I found 2 cursed magic lamps off a bones file, blessed
them, and got a GDSM and a tame djinni, who was pretty useless. A tool
shop with 3 magic markers on level 6 was also pretty useful.

I did the quest, which was lamer than I expected. I didn't get the Hunt
the Wumpus reference and I had to Wikipedia it. Scorpius was extremely
pathetic, and I left without much further ado. I used maybe 10-20k
turns to scour the dungeon for an instrument, and finally encountered a
trio of sergents. Going upstairs from the castle, I accidentally
entered Medusa's lair without blindfolding myself. Fortunately, she
stoned herself off of my Longbow before I was done in, so I survived
that encounter.

Things got more interesting at the castle. I used the drawbridge to
crush most of my enemies, and got the wand of wishing. I had GDSM and
GoP already, and I checked the storerooms for anything I might need. I
got all the flavours of boots, so I didn't need a wish for that.
Instead I got 2 blessed scrolls of charging and 2 blessed scrolls of
genocide, and got rid of h and L immediately. c and P went for
insta-death prevention, and I think I also did in H and T just for
their annoyance factor.

Downstairs I figured that I really needed a melee weapon, as bashing
things with my +7 Longbow of Diana as I'd been doing since the quest
didn't seem very prudent. I used my wand of wishing, now at (1:1) for
Magicbane, which I got on the first try. I wanted a light source and I
considered a magic lamp or perhaps Sunsword, but I decided that neither
were too important. But having a wish to burn, I used it on a blessed
figurine of an Archon for the first time. The one that appeared was
carrying a Sunsword!

With Vorpal Bubba at my side I cleared the dungeon pretty easily. I
accidentally shot four arrows into him in Orcus's town, so when the
unicorn horn I tossed to him hit him, he became untame. As I had the
spell of charm monster, I dumped my mana a few attempts, but as I was a
level 18 ranger with low intelligence and 88% fail and he was an
Archon, obviously my attempts were futile.

I trekked on without him, grabbing the loot in Vlad's tower and cutting
out a course through Gehennom. This game had gotten so boring that I
considered #quitting, but I managed to pull through. I slew Rodney with
the one wand of death that I had, Orcus having emptied his on me and
escaped upstairs. He would become a nuisance as I was making the run,
going upstairs several times until I finally managed to plant an arrow
up his a**.

The Sanctum wasn't too eventful. I dished out damage with Magicbane and
the Longbow's arrows, though I took a few hits of spell beams when I
wasn't wielding the bow. I was short on holy water so I used up my last
charge of cancellation on a few useless potions, and headed off.

The only real danger I encountered on my way was an Archon in Bigroom.
He followed me up a few levels, constantly bashing and stunning me, but
my AC was low enough for me to shrug it off. I eventually got annoyed
and teleported myself to the up stairs with a wand, having had teleport
control the whole time but not teleportitis.

The planes were easy, as I'd collected scrolls of gold detection. I
didn't do any fighting on the plane of Earth except for blasting the
Wizard, and air was relatively simple - I teleported the air elementals
away. There was an Archon on fire, but I used a confused gold mapping
to run to the portal and blindfolded myself to make it easier. Water
took a while, and I just floated around until I located the portal.

I landed in the Astral Plane and located the Riders. As usual, it was
Death, Pestilence, and Famine (in that order, I mean). I went to Famine
first, but as I was unable to stop him with my attack wands, I finally
used my wand of death, now at (0:3), on him. The crowd at the door was
thick, so I put on conflict. Mars bogged me down with angels, but they
were relatively weak. Famine revived, and I zapped my wand of death
again before I realized I was stunned, and it went through the door. At
least it killed a few priests for me. I applied my unicorn horn and
used my last charge on Famine, then charged through to the altar.

It was chaotic. But here my quest really began: The quest to compile a
version with the dumplog patch on winxp! It was long and tedious, and
there was no dumplog, but I succeeded, so here's the dumplog for the
game, at least:

